cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use telegram-mcp-kit in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "telegram-mcp-kit"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/telegram-mcp-kit"
url: "https://github.com/tonydzi/telegram-mcp-kit"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A setup path, production patches and a gotcha list for connecting an MCP client (Claude
  Code, Claude Desktop, Codex) to a personal Telegram account through the MTProto
  user-account server chigwell/telegram-mcp. Ships a shared HTTP/SSE daemon transport
  instead of one stdio copy per session, the tools daily agent work actually needs (dialog
  and global message search, incremental polling, t.me link resolution, unread mentions,
  media search), multi-account support, a Windows launcher and watchdog, and a security
  page on what handing an assistant a user-account session really grants. Upstream code is
  not vendored; the kit ships patches against it.
keywords:
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - telegram
  - mtproto
  - claude-code
  - agent-tooling
